sult\":\"  async def run(self, trace):\\n    total = await token_count(trace)\\n    await self._generate(\\n      trace,\\n      on_progress=lambda sent, _: _progress.append(sent / total),\\n    )\\n    await self._finalize()   # server-side grader, ~30s on a long trace\\n    _progress.append(1.0)\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"say\",\"text\":\"It isn't hanging. `on_progress` reaches 100% when the last token leaves the model, but `_finalize()` then waits on a server-side grader pass that takes ~30s on a long trace. The bar sits at 99% (rounding) with no indication anything is still happening, so people assume it hung and cancel.\\n\\nSo it's a **reporting** bug, not a generation bug — which also explains why it only shows up on long traces and why the runs that \\\"failed\\\" are actually graded and present in the store.\\n\\n\"},{\"kind\":\"usage\",\"input\":12600,\"output\":358,\"cache_read\":8400,\"cache_write\":1020,\"thought\":140},{\"kind\":\"say\",\"text\":\"I've moved HX-118 to **in progress**, retitled it to name the real cause, and linked HX-121 as a duplicate. The fix is a distinct grading-pending state rather than a progress percentage — Priya already has hybrid retrieval open in **retriever #88**, so the reporting fix can land beside it rather than starting a second PR.\"},{\"kind\":\"usage\",\"input\":13900,\"output\":188,\"cache_read\":12100,\"cache_write\":210}]}]";

