20001,\"number\":412,\"title\":\"Cap eval-run token budget per model family\",\"body\":\"Eval runs share one org-wide token pool, so a Haiku sweep can starve an Opus grading job that started later.\\n\\nThis puts a per-family cap behind `EvalBudget` — Sonnet 200k, Haiku 80k, Opus 400k — and surfaces remaining tokens on the run card.\\n\\n- [x] `EvalBudget` / `TokenLedger`\\n- [x] Caps per model family\\n- [x] Remaining-tokens chip on the run card\\n- [ ] Decide what happens when two evals share one run-group id\",\"state\":\"open\",\"is_draft\":false,\"author\":{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"},\"created_at\":\"@-3d\",\"updated_at\":\"@-4h\",\"repo_full_name\":\"helix/evalkit\",\"html_url\":\"https://example.invalid/helix/evalkit/pull/412\",\"external_id\":\"PR_412\",\"head_sha\":\"9f2c1ab7e4d05c3b8a61f7d2e0c94b5a7d13e6f8\",\"head_ref\":\"diego/eval-budget\",\"base_ref\":\"main\",\"base_sha\":\"1a7de90c4b28f6350e9d1c8b7a4f2e6d09c3b5a1\",\"requested_reviewers\":[{\"login\":\"maya-ok\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Maya Okonkwo\"}],\"requested_team_slugs\":[],\"assignees\":[{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"}],\"labels\":[{\"name\":\"enhancement\",\"color\":\"a2eeef\",\"description\":\"New feature or request\"}],\"reviewed_by_me\":false,\"reactions\":[{\"content\":\"THUMBS_UP\",\"emoji\":\"👍\",\"count\":2,\"user_reacted\":false,\"usernames\":[\"maya-ok\",\"priya-r\"]}],\"changed_files\":3,\"commits_count\":4,\"additions\":118,\"deletions\":26,\"comments_count\":3,\"checks_status\":\"passing\",\"mergeable_state\":\"clean\",\"review_decision\":\"reviewRequired\"},\"diff\":\"diff --git a/evalkit/budget.py b/evalkit/budget.py\\nindex 3f1a9c2..9f2c1ab 100644\\n--- a/evalkit/budget.py\\n+++ b/evalkit/budget.py\\n@@ -1,14 +1,42 @@\\n class EvalBudget:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"All spend math goes through the ledger so the run card, the\\n+    grader and the tests share one definition of remaining tokens.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\n+    def __init__(self, ledger):\\n+        self._ledger = ledger\\n+\\n     def remaining(self, family, run_group_id):\\n-        return 250_000 - self._spent\\n+        return self._cap(family) - self._ledger.spent(family)\\n+\\n+    def _cap(self, family):\\n+        return {\\n+            \\\"sonnet\\\": 200_000,\\n+            \\\"haiku\\\": 80_000,\\n+            \\\"opus\\\": 400_000,\\n+        }[family]\\n+\\n+\\n+class TokenLedger:\\n+    \\\"\\\"\\\"One definition of spend, injectable for tests.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+\\n+    def __init__(self, now=None):\\n+        self._now = now or (lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc))\\n+        self._rows = []\\n+\\n+    def record(self, family, tokens):\\n+        self._rows.append((family, tokens, self._now()))\\n+\\n+    def spent(self, family):\\n+        return sum(t for f, t, _ in self._rows if f == family)\\n\",\"files\":[{\"filename\":\"evalkit/budget.py\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":42,\"deletions\":8,\"patch\":\"@@ -1,14 +1,42 @@\\n class EvalBudget:\\n+    def __init__(self, ledger):\\n+        self._ledger = ledger\\n+\\n     def remaining(self, family, run_group_id):\\n-        return 250_000 - self._spent\\n+        return self._cap(family) - self._ledger.spent(family)\",\"viewed_state\":\"unviewed\"},{\"filename\":\"tests/evalkit/test_budget.py\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":68,\"deletions\":10,\"patch\":\"@@ -12,6 +12,18 @@\\n+def test_haiku_cap_is_80k():\\n+    assert budget.remaining(\\\"haiku\\\", \\\"g1\\\") == 80_000\\n+\\n+def test_a_cap_never_goes_negative():\\n+    ledger.record(\\\"haiku\\\", 90_000)\\n+    assert budget.remaining(\\\"haiku\\\", \\\"g1\\\") >= 0\",\"viewed_state\":\"unviewed\"},{\"filename\":\"CHANGELOG.md\",\"status\":\"modified\",\"additions\":8,\"deletions\":8,\"patch\":\"@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@\\n # Changelog\\n \\n-## Unreleased\\n+## Unreleased\\n+- Eval runs cap tokens per model family (Sonnet 200k, Haiku 80k, Opus 400k).\",\"viewed_state\":\"viewed\"}],\"commits\":[{\"sha\":\"1a7de90c4b28f6350e9d1c8b7a4f2e6d09c3b5a1\",\"message\":\"Introduce TokenLedger behind EvalBudget\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"},\"date\":\"@-3d\"},{\"sha\":\"4c8b2f19a7d360e5c1b98a2d4f70e6c3b5a91d82\",\"message\":\"Cap remaining tokens per model family\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"},\"date\":\"@-2d\"},{\"sha\":\"7e3a5d81c92b4f06a7d5e8c1b3f92a604d7c8e15\",\"message\":\"Pin the Haiku and Opus caps in tests\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"},\"date\":\"@-2d\"},{\"sha\":\"9f2c1ab7e4d05c3b8a61f7d2e0c94b5a7d13e6f8\",\"message\":\"Changelog\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"},\"date\":\"@-4h\"}],\"reviews\":[{\"id\":9001,\"state\":\"commented\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"ravi\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Ravi (AI)\"},\"body\":\"Reviewed 3 files (+118/−26).\\n\\n**What this does.** Eval runs stop sharing one org-wide pool: `remaining` now derives each family's cap through `TokenLedger` — Sonnet 200k, Haiku 80k, Opus 400k — so the run card, the grader and the tests share one definition of remaining tokens. That part is correct and I have no notes on it.\\n\\n**Blocking (1).** The calculation is keyed on the family alone. Two evals can share a run-group id — a nightly sweep and an ad-hoc grade kicked off the same hour — and `evalkit/extensions.py:71` recomputes through this same path after a retry is recorded, so one eval's spend burns the *other* run's remaining budget everywhere it renders. This is the open question in the PR body and it is still unresolved: the ledger needs the run-group id in the key.\\n\\n**Nits (3).**\\n- `_cap` / `spent` — the most-scrutinized math in the PR under the least searchable names. `cap_for` / `spent_for` say what they do.\\n- Haiku (80k) and Opus (400k) each have a pinning test; Sonnet (200k) is the one cap with a billing consequence when it slips, and it has none.\\n- The ledger never resets at UTC midnight, so a run that straddles the day keeps yesterday's spend. Fine if deliberate — say so where the caps are declared.\\n\\nApproving once the shared run-group race is addressed — the rest looks correct.\",\"submitted_at\":\"@-5h\",\"reactions\":[]}],\"review_comments\":[{\"id\":8801,\"body\":\"Two evals can share a run-group id — a nightly sweep and an ad-hoc grade kicked off the same hour. `remaining` resolves from the family alone, so once a retry is recorded on one run, the other eval's remaining tokens drop too. I think this is the \\\"budget moved on its own\\\" report.\\n\\nCould the ledger take the run-group id and resolve spend per group, so a retry on one never burns the other?\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"maya-ok\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Maya Okonkwo\"},\"path\":\"evalkit/budget.py\",\"position\":9,\"created_at\":\"@-6h\",\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"diff_hunk\":\"@@ -1,14 +1,42 @@\\n     def remaining(self, family, run_group_id):\",\"line\":9,\"thread_id\":\"thread-412-1\",\"reactions\":[{\"content\":\"EYES\",\"emoji\":\"👀\",\"count\":1,\"user_reacted\":false,\"usernames\":[\"dferrer\"]}]},{\"id\":8802,\"body\":\"Good catch — I'll key the ledger by the run-group id so each eval resolves its own spend. In this PR, not a follow-up.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"dferrer\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Diego Ferrer\"},\"path\":\"evalkit/budget.py\",\"position\":9,\"created_at\":\"@-5h\",\"side\":\"RIGHT\",\"in_reply_to_id\":8801,\"diff_hunk\":\"\",\"line\":9,\"thread_id\":\"thread-412-1\",\"reactions\":[]}],\"issue_comments\":[{\"id\":7701,\"body\":\"Rendering note while it's fresh: once a family is exhausted, \\\"0 tokens remaining\\\" reads like the run is still live. Show exhausted ones as \\\"Budget exhausted\\\" in the danger tone and stop counting down — otherwise we teach people to ignore the chip.\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"priya-r\",\"avatar_url\":\"\",\"name\":\"Priya Raman\"},\